1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,630
FTX customers have been paid back one hundred and five per cent.

2
00:00:04,983 --> 00:00:08,140
Its founder is serving twenty-five years.

3
00:00:08,483 --> 00:00:10,936
So why didn't the repayment matter?

4
00:00:11,283 --> 00:00:13,971
An appeals court answered in June.

5
00:00:14,316 --> 00:00:16,492
We'll read you its key sentence.

6
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:20,945
The short answer: the fraud was complete when the money moved.

7
00:00:21,349 --> 00:00:25,147
Believing customers would be repaid was no defence.

8
00:00:25,549 --> 00:00:29,153
And that hundred and five per cent was counted at a

9
00:00:29,153 --> 00:00:34,311
bitcoin price of sixteen thousand, eight hundred and seventy-one dollars.

10
00:00:34,983 --> 00:00:38,780
The price on the day FTX filed for bankruptcy.

11
00:00:39,216 --> 00:00:43,767
This is FTX from the court record: the code, the run, the trial,

12
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:48,532
the repayments, and a petition now waiting at the US Supreme Court.

13
00:00:49,216 --> 00:00:52,309
Where something is only alleged, we'll say so.

14
00:00:52,916 --> 00:00:53,850
Chapter one.

15
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:55,796
Two companies, one owner.

16
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,318
FTX was a crypto exchange.

17
00:00:58,318 --> 00:01:01,739
Sam Bankman-Fried ran it as chief executive

18
00:01:01,739 --> 00:01:04,682
from its founding in twenty nineteen.

19
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:10,218
He also controlled a trading firm, Alameda Research, founded in

20
00:01:10,218 --> 00:01:15,086
twenty seventeen and co-owned with FTX's co-founder, Gary Wang.

21
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:19,213
The appeals court describes Alameda as FTX's

22
00:01:19,213 --> 00:01:22,519
largest customer and primary market maker.

23
00:01:23,183 --> 00:01:27,543
So the people who ran the exchange also owned its biggest trader.

24
00:01:27,543 --> 00:01:29,690
That is where this story starts.

25
00:01:30,283 --> 00:01:34,169
At trial, Gary Wang described special privileges

26
00:01:34,169 --> 00:01:36,922
built into FTX's code for Alameda.

27
00:01:37,616 --> 00:01:43,024
According to that testimony, as the court summarises it, those privileges gave

28
00:01:43,024 --> 00:01:47,808
Alameda a sixty-five billion dollar line of credit from the exchange.

29
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:51,932
The SEC alleged Alameda was also exempted

30
00:01:51,932 --> 00:01:55,801
from certain key FTX risk mitigation measures.

31
00:01:56,483 --> 00:02:02,351
After the verdict, prosecutors said he directed co-conspirators to alter FTX's

32
00:02:02,351 --> 00:02:07,693
code so Alameda could withdraw effectively unlimited amounts of crypto.

33
00:02:08,383 --> 00:02:09,407
Chapter two.

34
00:02:09,407 --> 00:02:10,431
The promise.

35
00:02:10,883 --> 00:02:15,255
Since at least May twenty nineteen, the SEC said, FTX raised

36
00:02:15,255 --> 00:02:19,919
more than one point eight billion dollars from equity investors.

37
00:02:20,583 --> 00:02:24,852
The SEC's complaint says Bankman-Fried promoted FTX as

38
00:02:24,852 --> 00:02:29,201
a safe, responsible crypto asset trading platform, with

39
00:02:29,201 --> 00:02:34,419
sophisticated, automated risk measures to protect customer assets.

40
00:02:35,183 --> 00:02:38,207
Behind that, the complaint alleged, was an

41
00:02:38,207 --> 00:02:42,023
undisclosed diversion of customers' funds to Alameda.

42
00:02:42,683 --> 00:02:47,738
The SEC's chair, Gary Gensler, said: we allege that Sam Bankman-Fried

43
00:02:47,738 --> 00:02:51,548
built a house of cards on a foundation of deception.

44
00:02:52,216 --> 00:02:54,311
Those were civil allegations.

45
00:02:54,311 --> 00:02:57,635
The criminal findings came later, from a jury.

46
00:02:58,250 --> 00:02:59,403
Chapter three.

47
00:02:59,403 --> 00:03:01,215
Nine days in November.

48
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:05,215
On the second of November twenty twenty-two, a crypto

49
00:03:05,215 --> 00:03:09,049
news site published a version of Alameda's balance sheet.

50
00:03:09,716 --> 00:03:15,327
The appeals court says that triggered widespread customer withdrawals from FTX.

51
00:03:15,916 --> 00:03:19,169
On the eleventh of November, Bankman-Fried was

52
00:03:19,169 --> 00:03:21,855
replaced and FTX filed for bankruptcy.

53
00:03:21,855 --> 00:03:25,744
It could no longer meet customers' withdrawal requests.

54
00:03:26,416 --> 00:03:31,543
At his trial, Bankman-Fried testified that he was surprised to learn of

55
00:03:31,543 --> 00:03:37,608
Alameda's eight billion dollar negative balance on FTX in October twenty twenty-two.

56
00:03:38,283 --> 00:03:40,780
The new chief executive was John J.

57
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:44,704
Ray the third, who had worked on the clean-up of Enron.

58
00:03:45,316 --> 00:03:48,584
Six days later he filed a sworn declaration.

59
00:03:48,584 --> 00:03:51,183
He wrote: never in my career have I

60
00:03:51,183 --> 00:03:54,970
seen such a complete failure of corporate controls.

61
00:03:55,650 --> 00:04:00,897
He described the absence of an accurate list of bank accounts and signatories,

62
00:04:00,897 --> 00:04:05,204
and said the group did not keep centralised control of its cash.

63
00:04:05,883 --> 00:04:09,166
Corporate money, he said, had bought homes and

64
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:12,592
other personal items for employees and advisors.

65
00:04:12,592 --> 00:04:17,374
Some payments were approved by responding with personalised emojis.

66
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:23,212
And Bankman-Fried, he said, used messaging apps set to auto-delete after a

67
00:04:23,212 --> 00:04:27,537
short period of time, and encouraged employees to do the same.

68
00:04:28,216 --> 00:04:29,281
Chapter four.

69
00:04:29,281 --> 00:04:30,264
The verdict.

70
00:04:30,716 --> 00:04:33,443
The trial in Manhattan ran four weeks.

71
00:04:33,443 --> 00:04:39,400
Three of his inner circle testified under cooperation agreements: Caroline Ellison,

72
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:43,850
Gary Wang, and FTX's former head of engineering, Nishad Singh.

73
00:04:44,516 --> 00:04:48,992
On the second of November twenty twenty-three, the jury convicted

74
00:04:48,992 --> 00:04:52,298
him on all seven counts of fraud and conspiracy.

75
00:04:52,983 --> 00:04:57,780
The US Attorney, Damian Williams, said the industry might be new, but,

76
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:01,618
in his words, this kind of corruption is as old as time.

77
00:05:02,283 --> 00:05:07,765
On the twenty-eighth of March twenty twenty-four, Judge Lewis Kaplan sentenced him

78
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:12,712
to twenty-five years, with forfeiture of more than eleven billion dollars.

79
00:05:13,383 --> 00:05:17,696
Prosecutors put the losses at more than eight billion dollars

80
00:05:17,696 --> 00:05:22,222
of customers' money, one point seven billion from FTX investors,

81
00:05:22,222 --> 00:05:25,828
and one point three billion from Alameda's lenders.

82
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:29,989
The defence argued customers had lost no money.

83
00:05:29,989 --> 00:05:32,743
Reuters reported that the judge called

84
00:05:32,743 --> 00:05:36,366
that misleading, logically flawed and speculative.

85
00:05:37,049 --> 00:05:41,534
He compared it to a thief who takes his loot to Las Vegas and wins.

86
00:05:41,534 --> 00:05:45,817
Repaying the loss from the winnings, he said, earns no discount.

87
00:05:46,416 --> 00:05:47,403
Chapter five.

88
00:05:47,403 --> 00:05:48,997
The money comes back.

89
00:05:49,449 --> 00:05:54,402
In October twenty twenty-four, the Delaware bankruptcy court confirmed

90
00:05:54,402 --> 00:05:58,577
FTX's repayment plan, with between fourteen point seven and

91
00:05:58,577 --> 00:06:02,044
sixteen point five billion dollars to distribute.

92
00:06:02,783 --> 00:06:07,714
FTX said ninety-eight per cent of its creditors, by number, would receive

93
00:06:07,714 --> 00:06:12,038
about one hundred and nineteen per cent of their allowed claims.

94
00:06:12,716 --> 00:06:14,325
Then came the payments.

95
00:06:14,325 --> 00:06:17,893
After the fourth round, in March twenty twenty-six,

96
00:06:17,893 --> 00:06:21,531
international customers were at ninety-six per cent.

97
00:06:21,531 --> 00:06:26,918
The fifth round, in July, took both customer classes to one hundred and five.

98
00:06:27,583 --> 00:06:31,312
The Block reports nearly ten billion dollars has gone to

99
00:06:31,312 --> 00:06:36,306
creditors and other claimants since repayments began in twenty twenty-five.

100
00:06:36,983 --> 00:06:38,818
So were customers made whole?

101
00:06:38,818 --> 00:06:40,780
That depends on what you count.

102
00:06:41,383 --> 00:06:46,550
In a twenty twenty-four ruling, Judge John Dorsey wrote that claims must be

103
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:51,511
valued as of the petition date, as if the bankruptcy had never occurred.

104
00:06:52,183 --> 00:06:56,417
For FTX, that was the eleventh of November twenty twenty-two.

105
00:06:56,417 --> 00:07:01,484
Coins held that day were turned into a dollar figure at that day's price.

106
00:07:02,083 --> 00:07:06,778
As the crypto outlet Unchained put it, a creditor repaid at one hundred

107
00:07:06,778 --> 00:07:11,275
and five per cent has still missed most of the market's climb since.

108
00:07:11,949 --> 00:07:13,029
Chapter six.

109
00:07:13,029 --> 00:07:14,019
The appeal.

110
00:07:14,483 --> 00:07:16,048
Bankman-Fried appealed.

111
00:07:16,048 --> 00:07:20,402
On the twelfth of June twenty twenty-six, a three-judge panel of

112
00:07:20,402 --> 00:07:25,572
the Second Circuit affirmed the conviction, the sentence and the forfeiture.

113
00:07:26,249 --> 00:07:30,956
One of his central complaints was evidence the jury never heard: that

114
00:07:30,956 --> 00:07:35,867
customers would be repaid, and that his investments later rose in value.

115
00:07:36,549 --> 00:07:38,990
Here is the sentence we promised.

116
00:07:38,990 --> 00:07:41,875
FTX customers were defrauded as soon as

117
00:07:41,875 --> 00:07:45,500
Bankman-Fried transferred their money to Alameda.

118
00:07:46,183 --> 00:07:49,303
The trial judge had ruled it immaterial as a

119
00:07:49,303 --> 00:07:52,351
matter of law whether he intended to repay.

120
00:07:52,351 --> 00:07:54,762
The appeals court agreed, and said

121
00:07:54,762 --> 00:07:58,094
the law covers even temporary misappropriation.

122
00:07:58,849 --> 00:08:02,955
Whether the assets he bought appreciated in value, the judges

123
00:08:02,955 --> 00:08:06,590
wrote, is irrelevant as to whether he committed fraud.

124
00:08:07,249 --> 00:08:11,576
And they described him using FTX as his own personal piggy

125
00:08:11,576 --> 00:08:17,991
bank, spending customer funds on real estate, political contributions and investments.

126
00:08:18,649 --> 00:08:19,663
It is not over.

127
00:08:19,663 --> 00:08:24,665
On the tenth of September, he asked the US Supreme Court to hear his case.

128
00:08:25,249 --> 00:08:28,290
Five amicus briefs followed in October, one

129
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:31,259
from a group of bankruptcy law professors.

130
00:08:31,259 --> 00:08:35,642
The government's response is due on the sixteenth of December.

131
00:08:35,642 --> 00:08:39,813
The justices have not yet decided whether to take the case.

132
00:08:40,483 --> 00:08:43,327
Here is what we take from the paperwork.

133
00:08:43,327 --> 00:08:45,176
This part is our analysis.

134
00:08:45,616 --> 00:08:49,328
FTX has been judged on two different ledgers.

135
00:08:49,916 --> 00:08:54,221
The criminal ledger asks whether money was taken by deception.

136
00:08:54,221 --> 00:08:57,276
The courts said yes, at the moment it moved.

137
00:08:57,883 --> 00:09:01,100
The bankruptcy ledger asks what each customer was

138
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:03,726
owed, in dollars, on the day it stopped.

139
00:09:03,726 --> 00:09:07,993
That is the figure being repaid at one hundred and five per cent.

140
00:09:08,649 --> 00:09:10,125
Both numbers are true.

141
00:09:10,125 --> 00:09:12,270
Neither is the same as the coins

142
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:15,622
customers believed were sitting in their accounts.

143
00:09:16,283 --> 00:09:20,682
The useful lesson: before you leave money on any platform, ask who else

144
00:09:20,682 --> 00:09:25,266
can draw on it, whether customer assets are kept separate, and who checks.

145
00:09:25,916 --> 00:09:27,825
FTX's run took nine days.

146
00:09:27,825 --> 00:09:31,642
Silicon Valley Bank's customers withdrew more than

147
00:09:31,642 --> 00:09:34,544
forty billion dollars in a single day.

148
00:09:35,216 --> 00:09:39,008
Next on Filed Under Failure: Northern Rock and Silicon

149
00:09:39,008 --> 00:09:42,309
Valley Bank, two bank runs sixteen years apart.

150
00:09:42,309 --> 00:09:45,258
Subscribe so the next case file finds you.
